            {"id": "b", "text": "Impact dot-matrix printers are the only printer type capable of printing on multi-layer carbon copy (NCR) forms", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. Impact printing physically strikes the paper/ribbon stack, creating pressure that transfers marks through multiple layers. This is the defining capability for multi-part NCR (No Carbon Required) forms. Laser, inkjet, dye-sub, and thermal printers do not physically strike the paper and cannot make impressions on carbon copy or pressure-sensitive lower layers."},
